    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0107",
      "sequence": 119,
      "meaning": "Kāma’s foe sits as beautifully as serenity embodied. Recognizing the good moment, Mother Bhavānī approaches Śambhu. Knowing his beloved, Hara honors her deeply and gives her a seat on his left. Seated joyfully beside Śiva, she remembers her former birth. Perceiving especially favorable love in her husband’s heart, Umā smiles and asks in tender words for the story that benefits every world. She addresses Viśvanātha, her Lord and Tripura’s foe, whose glory is renowned across the three worlds and whose lotus feet every moving and unmoving being, nāga, human and god serves. Śiva is mighty, omniscient, an abode of every art and virtue, a treasury of yoga, knowledge and detachment, and by name a wish-tree for those who bow.",
