    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0110",
      "sequence": 122,
      "meaning": "Though a woman is traditionally said not to be entitled to hidden teaching, Pārvatī says she is Śiva’s servant in mind, deed and speech, and saints do not conceal even profound truth when they find a distressed yet qualified seeker. In deep yearning she asks the divine Lord compassionately to tell Raghupati’s story: first, why qualityless Brahman assumed a qualified body; then Rāma’s incarnation and generous childhood deeds; how he married Jānakī; what fault made him leave the kingdom; his countless forest deeds and how he killed Rāvaṇa; his many pastimes after taking the throne; and finally the wonder by which merciful Rāma, jewel of Raghu’s line, went to his own abode with his people.",
